<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!-- Helper processes entitlements.

         IMPORTANT — allow-jit MUST be present here.
         In Electron's multi-process architecture, V8 runs inside each
         "Live Music Coder Helper (Renderer)" process, NOT in the main
         browser process. Without allow-jit, the renderer SIGTRAPs during
         v8::Isolate::Initialize → cppgc::PersistentRegionLock → and the
         window stays blank ("black screen" symptom). This was the v1.0.1
         regression: a previous CLAUDE.md note incorrectly claimed only
         the main app needs JIT, so the helper plist was created without
         it. See the renderer crash report:
         ~/Library/Logs/DiagnosticReports/Live Music Coder Helper (Renderer)*.ips
         for the matching v8 crash trace. -->
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
    <true/>
    <!-- REMOVED 2026-08-17, all three unused:
         · device.microphone + device.audio-input — nothing in src/ ever calls
           getUserMedia (0 hits). Keeping them meant a hostile evaluated pattern
           could trigger a TCC prompt attributed to a notarized MUSIC app, which
           is the most plausible prompt a user of this app will ever accept.
           src/lib/audio/recorder.ts taps the internal graph, never an input device.
         · cs.allow-dyld-environment-variables — unnecessary for Electron. Not a
           live hole (disable-library-validation is absent and the hardened
           runtime is on, so injection is still rejected), but it is privilege
           nobody asked for.
         Removing device.microphone also lets NSMicrophoneUsageDescription go
         from the Info.plist once the next release is cut. -->
    <key>com.apple.security.inherit</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
